1
00:00:13,119 --> 00:00:14,359
Mr. Zhao, you've got some

2
00:00:14,359 --> 00:00:15,640
serious dark circles.

3
00:00:16,359 --> 00:00:18,000
Didn't sleep well last night?

4
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:22,120
Yu Song,

5
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,160
I really underestimated you.

6
00:00:24,719 --> 00:00:26,320
But don't get ahead of yourself.

7
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:29,359
Even if I agree to your terms,

8
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,519
you might not get the files.

9
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:34,240
Song Huan grew this powerful

10
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,799
despite Song Huaishan holding her back.

11
00:00:36,359 --> 00:00:37,399
She's not easy to deal with.

12
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:40,880
If I can make this offer,

13
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:42,600
I've got my ways.

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:56,799
Interesting.

15
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,399
A fox and a viper.

16
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,000
I'm curious to see

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,359
who takes the other out first,

18
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:06,159
you or Song Huan.

19
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,146
=Dear Song=

20
00:01:09,173 --> 00:01:11,460
=Episode 6=
(The Clash of Fangs)

21
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:13,600
(The Song Family Tree)

22
00:01:19,626 --> 00:01:21,690
(Video Conference in Progress)

23
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,400
(4 AM.)

24
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,760
(International meeting.)

25
00:01:35,239 --> 00:01:36,239
(6 AM.)

26
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,719
(Keeping in shape.)

27
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:44,519
Ms. Song Huan, take care.

28
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,239
(8 AM.)

29
00:01:48,239 --> 00:01:49,560
(Off to work.)

30
00:01:50,439 --> 00:01:51,719
Morning, Ms. Song Huan.

31
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:52,186
(Song Group)

32
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,359
Morning, Ms. Song Huan.

33
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:56,079
(Morning, Ms. Song Huan.)

34
00:01:58,170 --> 00:01:59,986
(General Office)

35
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,480
(The Song Family Tree)

36
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,919
From international meetings
halfway across the globe

37
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:24,439
to clocking out,

38
00:02:24,719 --> 00:02:26,159
that's 13 appointments a day.

39
00:02:26,159 --> 00:02:28,039
Four hours of sleep.

40
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,919
The queen really has endless energy.

41
00:02:31,039 --> 00:02:32,319
But that's exactly why

42
00:02:32,439 --> 00:02:33,360
she's so hard to get close to.

43
00:02:33,639 --> 00:02:35,560
If I plot long enough,

44
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:37,360
I will find an opening.

45
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,199
So, my dear Ms. Yu,

46
00:02:44,639 --> 00:02:45,879
don't you think you should spare

47
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:48,199
some energy for me while you're waiting?

48
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,199
(Tomorrow at 8 AM.)

49
00:03:17,319 --> 00:03:18,520
(Hot spring project meeting.)

50
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,120
(No one is allowed to be late.)

51
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:22,520
I'll owe you tonight.

52
00:03:22,719 --> 00:03:24,520
I'll pay you back with interest.

53
00:03:42,746 --> 00:03:45,020
(GangA 88555)

54
00:03:45,639 --> 00:03:46,360
Ms. Song Huan,

55
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,919
Zhang says something he ate this morning
upset his stomach.

56
00:03:47,919 --> 00:03:49,360
He'll be here in about half an hour.

57
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,199
I need to be at the office
in 15 minutes.

58
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,599
I'd appreciate a ride.

59
00:03:53,599 --> 00:03:54,560
Sorry, Ms. Song Huan.

60
00:03:54,759 --> 00:03:55,680
Mr. Song told me

61
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,639
to pick him up at the golf course.

62
00:03:57,919 --> 00:03:59,520
That's the opposite direction
from the office.

63
00:04:03,546 --> 00:04:04,666
(GangA 66688)

64
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,666
(Future Center)

65
00:04:17,319 --> 00:04:18,399
Ms. Song Huan.

66
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,879
So clumsy.

67
00:04:20,319 --> 00:04:21,839
Did Song Cheng teach you that, too?

68
00:04:22,199 --> 00:04:23,519
Sorry, Ms. Song Huan.

69
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,720
Ms. Song Cheng wanted tofu soup.

70
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,360
And it had to be from the place
on Yuyang Road.

71
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,360
It's a bit far.

72
00:04:28,399 --> 00:04:30,040
So I drove there myself.

73
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,439
I was afraid the soup would get cold.

74
00:04:31,439 --> 00:04:32,160
So...

75
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,519
You can drive?

76
00:04:35,519 --> 00:04:36,879
Ms. Song Huan needs to go somewhere.

77
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:37,920
Give her a ride.

78
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:38,720
Consider it an apology.

79
00:04:39,519 --> 00:04:40,319
Okay.

80
00:04:41,319 --> 00:04:42,199
Give me the keys.

81
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,959
You work for Song Cheng.

82
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,759
So just take care of her.

83
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:58,959
And

84
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,480
tell Zhang

85
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,360
he's fired.

86
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:18,399
Looks like the laxatives in Zhang's tea
were wasted.

87
00:05:20,399 --> 00:05:22,439
He's been skimming gas money for years.

88
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,920
He thinks being older gives him
the right to push you around.

89
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:26,120
I don't care about the gas money,

90
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,240
but no one gets to pick on you.

91
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,560
But

92
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,920
Song Huan

93
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,920
really is hard to get close to.

94
00:05:36,519 --> 00:05:37,319
So what now?

95
00:05:37,839 --> 00:05:39,639
In Song Huan's eyes,
there are only two kinds of people.

96
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,839
People who are useful,

97
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:43,920
and worthless trash.

98
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,959
If I want to prove myself,

99
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:48,399
I have to impress her.

100
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,560
If I can get Song Cheng

101
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,160
taken seriously by the Song family,

102
00:05:52,639 --> 00:05:54,519
Song Huan will see my value on her own.

103
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,439
Ladies.

104
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,360
Fresh-baked cookies.

105
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,639
Take your time.

106
00:06:04,639 --> 00:06:05,319
Just put them there.

107
00:06:05,319 --> 00:06:06,199
Sure.

108
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,959
These have way too many calories.

109
00:06:07,959 --> 00:06:09,519
Eating them would make my Botox
go to waste.

110
00:06:10,199 --> 00:06:12,319
You always have to look your best, huh?

111
00:06:13,439 --> 00:06:15,040
They do look good.

112
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:16,639
Song Lin.

113
00:06:17,319 --> 00:06:18,160
I heard a while back

114
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,480
that your illegitimate half-sister

115
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,959
studied under a master woodcarver.

116
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,639
Are all those

117
00:06:22,639 --> 00:06:23,800
wood carvings done by her?

118
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:26,480
Yeah.

119
00:06:28,199 --> 00:06:30,120
That little rabbit looks cute.

120
00:06:30,199 --> 00:06:31,560
Go get it and show us.

121
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,160
Just a piece of wood.

122
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,560
What's there to see?

123
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:41,160
Check this out.

124
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,360
My new jade.

125
00:06:45,199 --> 00:06:47,040
We've seen plenty of fancy jewelry.

126
00:06:47,759 --> 00:06:49,279
But wood worth hundreds of thousands?

127
00:06:49,279 --> 00:06:50,720
That's a rarity.

128
00:06:51,759 --> 00:06:52,759
What,

129
00:06:52,759 --> 00:06:54,439
don't tell me
you don't dare bring it out.

130
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,519
Exactly.

131
00:06:55,519 --> 00:06:57,000
Why wouldn't I?

132
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,600
Ms. Chen.

133
00:07:00,439 --> 00:07:01,120
Ms. Chen!

134
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:02,800
Ms. Song Lin,

135
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,439
what is it?

136
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,079
Bring me

137
00:07:06,079 --> 00:07:06,920
that rabbit.

138
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:11,439
Ms. Song Lin,

139
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,240
Ms. Song Cheng is eating in her room.

140
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,839
If she comes out later and finds out...

141
00:07:15,839 --> 00:07:17,600
Why are you afraid of her?

142
00:07:17,759 --> 00:07:19,199
I'm not.

143
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:21,639
But she's got a loyal lapdog.

144
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,800
And when that dog goes mad,

145
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,120
it really bites.

146
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:27,040
I'm right here.

147
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,120
If she dares lay a finger on you,

148
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,360
I'll claw her face off!

149
00:07:30,759 --> 00:07:31,560
Go get it!

150
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,519
Got it.

151
00:07:35,399 --> 00:07:36,199
Go on, take a look.

152
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,040
It's really finely carved.

153
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,759
It's actually pretty cute.

154
00:07:43,279 --> 00:07:44,160
Let me see.

155
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,759
Yeah.

156
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,079
Then...

157
00:07:50,839 --> 00:07:52,120
Let's play with it!

158
00:07:52,879 --> 00:07:53,360
Lin.

159
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:54,439
Catch!

160
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:57,079
Little rabbit!

161
00:08:00,959 --> 00:08:02,160
Bunny.

162
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,160
Stop it!

163
00:08:05,199 --> 00:08:06,120
This rabbit

164
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:09,360
was carved from ivory wood
Dad brought back from Africa.

165
00:08:09,439 --> 00:08:11,319
Ivory wood is rare these days.

166
00:08:12,839 --> 00:08:13,399
Lin.

167
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:17,000
Why did you touch my stuff?

168
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,879
Oh.

169
00:08:22,079 --> 00:08:25,199
Having someone backing you up
sure makes a difference, huh?

170
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:28,079
Now you dare yell at me?

171
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,199
My mom

172
00:08:30,199 --> 00:08:32,600
is Dad's lawful wife.

173
00:08:32,879 --> 00:08:34,919
We both know what kind of woman
your mom is.

174
00:08:35,159 --> 00:08:36,960
I don't need to spell it out, do I?

175
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:40,399
You're a mistress's illegitimate child,
a dirty little secret.

176
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,679
You should hang your head in shame
for the rest of your life!

177
00:08:43,919 --> 00:08:46,919
Sounds like this thing
is actually worth something.

178
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,600
Mine now!

179
00:08:50,759 --> 00:08:51,879
Stop it!

180
00:08:54,799 --> 00:08:55,559
Ms. Song Cheng!

181
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,879
What are you looking at me for?

182
00:09:19,879 --> 00:09:21,240
You wanna bite me?

183
00:09:21,759 --> 00:09:23,120
I'm not Ms. Chen.

184
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,759
Even Song Cheng has to

185
00:09:25,759 --> 00:09:27,639
keep her head down in this house.

186
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,120
You're just a servant.

187
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:35,360
Know your place!

188
00:09:46,639 --> 00:09:47,519
(Lin.)

189
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,720
(You just got cosmetic injections.)

190
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,320
(You can't get angry.)

191
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,639
Right.

192
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:57,360
It cost tens of thousands.

193
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,399
Can't let it go to waste.

194
00:09:58,399 --> 00:09:59,159
(Right.)

195
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:01,159
Let's go dance in the living room.

196
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,279
My dad invited

197
00:10:02,279 --> 00:10:04,799
some very important guests
to tomorrow's banquet.

198
00:10:04,799 --> 00:10:08,399
He specifically told me
to nail the opening dance.

199
00:10:08,559 --> 00:10:11,159
I'm the face of the Song family.

200
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,960
Not like some people,

201
00:10:13,519 --> 00:10:15,960
who are like rotten wood.

202
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,519
Useless.

203
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:39,399
Ms. Song Cheng,

204
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,559
are we telling Mr. Song
about what happened today?

205
00:10:43,399 --> 00:10:45,039
If Dad wanted to do something about it,

206
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:46,720
he would've already.

207
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:49,440
This isn't the first time
this has happened.

208
00:10:50,519 --> 00:10:51,200
Why?

209
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:53,080
I've been so careful living

210
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,559
in this house.

211
00:10:55,159 --> 00:10:56,720
Why do they still treat me like this?

212
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:00,720
Ms. Song Cheng,

213
00:11:01,399 --> 00:11:02,600
hiding in the corner

214
00:11:03,159 --> 00:11:04,759
only lets those picking on you

215
00:11:04,759 --> 00:11:06,120
push you around even more.

216
00:11:07,559 --> 00:11:09,039
I'm sure you know better than I do

217
00:11:10,159 --> 00:11:11,720
how to hold your own in this family.

218
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:15,759
Of course I know.

219
00:11:16,679 --> 00:11:18,759
Dad's favor matters most.

220
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,679
Huan and Lin

221
00:11:20,679 --> 00:11:22,639
can both help him with business.

222
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:24,559
But I

223
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,559
can't do anything.

224
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,120
Is there anything you've wanted to do?

225
00:11:35,519 --> 00:11:36,320
Yu Song.

226
00:11:37,759 --> 00:11:38,840
What should I do?

227
00:11:39,519 --> 00:11:40,519
Help me.

228
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:45,639
Please?

229
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,879
What did they mean

230
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,519
about

231
00:11:56,519 --> 00:11:58,000
the family dinner

232
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,679
and the dance?

233
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,519
All I know is

234
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,960
Dad wants Lin to dance tomorrow
to seal a deal

235
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:08,840
with the Jinhai Chamber of Commerce.

236
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:11,039
If we can help Dad,

237
00:12:11,039 --> 00:12:12,720
he'll be really happy.

238
00:12:13,639 --> 00:12:15,639
(The president
of the Jinhai Chamber of Commerce)

239
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:16,799
(is Yu Qixian.)

240
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,720
(The Jinhai Chamber of Commerce
has influence throughout Nigang.)

241
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,720
(He built it all himself.)

242
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:24,679
(Looks like Song Huaishan wants to
use this chance to win Yu Qixian over)

243
00:12:24,679 --> 00:12:26,320
(and expand his own power.)

244
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,159
So

245
00:12:31,159 --> 00:12:33,600
if you can take Ms. Song Lin's place

246
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,039
on stage tomorrow

247
00:12:35,159 --> 00:12:36,600
and catch their eye,

248
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:39,440
Mr. Song will probably value you more.

249
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,559
But I can't even stand.

250
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,320
How am I supposed to dance?

251
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:46,240
Sometimes,

252
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:48,759
you don't need legs to stand up.

253
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:52,960
I've got a plan.

254
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,120
You wanna hear it?

255
00:12:57,530 --> 00:12:59,826
(Yu Qixian's Personal File)

256
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,759
He's got his eye
on a plot of land in the south.

257
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,799
He wants to build a horse ranch
with Yu Qixian.

258
00:13:05,519 --> 00:13:07,120
His real motive isn't the horse ranch.

259
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,440
A horse ranch?

260
00:13:09,799 --> 00:13:11,919
Just a front for an underground casino
that offers sexual services.

261
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,799
So he's having Song Lin
do the opening dance tomorrow night

262
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,440
to make Yu Qixian happy.

263
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,519
Dancing?

264
00:13:17,519 --> 00:13:18,320
Yeah.

265
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,399
Is this some new kind of
business tactic?

266
00:13:22,639 --> 00:13:24,559
I heard his wife passed away.

267
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,360
They met at the opera house.

268
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,320
Mm.

269
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:32,279
So, Detective,

270
00:13:32,279 --> 00:13:34,000
can you dig up some more for me?

271
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:37,000
Could you pay me half up front?

272
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:40,799
Will this do?

273
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,440
This job is really hard.

274
00:13:43,039 --> 00:13:44,240
That's probably not enough.

275
00:14:07,799 --> 00:14:08,759
(Ms. Song Cheng,)

276
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,320
(hiding in the corner)

277
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,240
(only lets those picking on you)

278
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,559
(push you around even more.)

279
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:16,360
(I'm sure you know better than I do)

280
00:14:17,039 --> 00:14:18,559
(how to hold your own in this family.)

281
00:14:44,799 --> 00:14:46,200
(People swimming against the current)

282
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:48,159
(have to grab
onto driftwood themselves.)

283
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,559
(If Song Cheng wants to hold her ground
in the Song family,)

